                                                                    30 1451
 Temperatures = 296 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 1600 2000 K.      30 1451
                                                                    30 1451
 Background                                                         30 1451
 ----------                                                         30 1451
                                                                    30 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics    30 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University. The thermal       30 1451
 scattering law data for graphite (perfect single crystal) were     30 1451
 developed using the ab initio lattice dynamics (AILD) method       30 1451
 [1,2]. The coherent elastic cross sections were calculated based   30 1451
 on the lattice constant obtained for AILD graphite. Ten            30 1451
 temperatures are available in this library. The LEAPR module from  30 1451
 the NJOY code system was used to produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data     30 1451
 for graphite. The coherent elastic data were prepared using the    30 1451
 cubic approximation in LEAPR/NJOY. By convention, MAT=31 and       30 1451
 ZA=131 are used for graphite.                                      30 1451
                                                                    30 1451
                                                                    30 1451
 References                                                         30 1451
 ----------                                                         30 1451
                                                                    30 1451
 1. A.I. Hawari, "Modern Techniques in Inelastic Thermal Neutron    30 1451
    Scattering Analysis," Nuclear Data Sheets 118 (2014) 172.       30 1451
 2. J.L. Wormald, A.I. Hawari "Thermal neutron scattering law       30 1451
    calculations using ab initio molecular dynamics", EPJ Web of    30 1451
    conferences 146, 13002 (2017)                                   30 1451
